1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,967
2:03 a.m. A man has suddenly become a philosopher.

2
00:00:05,967 --> 00:00:07,500
Bro… what did you just do?

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:10,800
Don't ask. Right now, I am a sage.

4
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,167
Your eyes were blazing red a minute ago.

5
00:00:13,167 --> 00:00:15,800
Which is why we research. Serious mode on.

6
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:17,467
Today: sage mode.

7
00:00:17,467 --> 00:00:20,633
Why do people go through all that chaos for a few seconds?

8
00:00:20,633 --> 00:00:24,900
One. Dopamine fires less for "I like it" and more for "I want it."

9
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:27,967
Chasing it: fireworks. Catching it: fizzle.

10
00:00:27,967 --> 00:00:31,000
So that's why a package is most exciting before you open it.

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,833
Two. Right after that moment, a hormone called prolactin spikes.

12
00:00:34,833 --> 00:00:37,333
One theory said it's the brain's brake pedal…

13
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:40,667
But in mice, blocking it didn't shorten the break at all.

14
00:00:40,667 --> 00:00:42,133
Then who's the culprit?

15
00:00:42,133 --> 00:00:43,167
Still under investigation.

16
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:48,833
Three. In one survey study, aroused men said yes to things they'd normally refuse.

17
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:51,600
And when calm, they had no idea how much they'd change.

18
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:54,767
Hot Me makes the mess. Cold Me cleans it up.

19
00:00:54,767 --> 00:00:58,867
Texts at 2 a.m., impulse buys…

20
00:00:58,867 --> 00:01:00,800
All the work of Hot Me.

21
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:05,900
Four. Over four in ten men and women said they've felt down for no reason afterward.

22
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:08,467
So it's not just me.

23
00:01:08,467 --> 00:01:12,700
Conclusion: we don't live for the few seconds. We live for the chase.

24
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:15,600
And the sage always shows up three minutes late.

25
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:18,600
So make big decisions in sage mode.

26
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:22,200
Honey, should I order that massage chair now?

27
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:24,500
Ask me again in sage mode.

28
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:27,800
(gulp) Limited edition… wait. I'll wait for sage mode.

29
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:28,933
Three minutes later.

30
00:01:28,933 --> 00:01:29,867
…Purchase.

31
00:01:29,867 --> 00:01:33,433
Even a sage can't stop a geek.
